# The middle of three gates. `complete:fast` is type-check, lint and format check; this adds the
# unit suite; `complete:check` adds build, integration and contract on top.
#
# Around 35 seconds, which is the point: a hook slow enough to be worth skipping gets skipped, and
# a hook that gets bypassed protects nothing. The unit suite fits because it mocks its
# collaborators — 946 tests in ~17s.
#
# What stays out, deliberately: integration and contract. Both run `--runInBand` against a real
# in-memory Mongo over HTTP, so they cost minutes rather than seconds, and CI already runs each as
# its own parallel job.
#
# Before pushing (or opening a PR), run the full gate by hand: `npm run complete:check`.
npm run complete:commit
